mdl 1;
-- ============================================================================
-- mendixlabs/mxcli#1486 (ako/mxcli#1343): marketplace diff/update fail with
-- 'path too long' when unpacking under %TEMP%
-- ============================================================================
--
-- Symptom, reported against v0.26.0 on Windows 11 (Mendix 11.12.4):
--
--   Extracting module files into C:\Users\<user>\AppData\Local\Temp\mxdiff1185592798\target-ref
--   The specified file name or path is too long, or a component of the specified path is too long.
--
--   The same command succeeds with TMP=C:\mxt.
--
-- Root cause:
--   mx refuses to write any file whose path is 260 characters or longer, and
--   it does so itself (Mendix's FileSystem.OpenNewFileForWriting), so the
--   limit holds on Linux and macOS too. Measured with mx 11.12.1 on Linux:
--   module-import of a package with a 200-character entry succeeds under a
--   58-character directory and fails under a 59-character one, with exactly
--   the reported message; create-project of the blank app fails from a
--   78-character directory up.
--
--   The reference project was built in %TEMP%\mxdiff<10 digits>\target-ref.
--   The deepest bundled files are node_modules trees (181 characters in the
--   11.12.1 blank app, about 202 in NanoflowCommons 7.x), so for
--   NanoflowCommons 7.x that layout fits no user name at all.
--
-- After fix: references are built under the shortest directory the user owns
-- (%USERPROFILE%\.mxcli\t on Windows, /tmp on POSIX, or TMP/TMPDIR when
-- shorter), named in one letter beneath it; a remaining refusal says which
-- directory, how long, and what is left for the package.
--
-- Usage (Windows, a project with Nanoflow Commons 6.x installed):
--   mxcli marketplace diff <content-id> -p app.mpr --to 7.4.0
--   mxcli marketplace update <content-id> -p app.mpr --to 7.4.0 --save-edits ./local-edits
--   mxcli exec mdl-examples/bug-tests/1486-marketplace-work-dir-path-too-long.mdl -p app.mpr
-- Regression test with a real mx (Linux, mxbuild 11.12.1 cached):
--   go test -tags integration ./cmd/mxcli/marketplace/ -run TestPackageProject_BuildsUnderADeepTempDir
-- ============================================================================

-- After the update the module is listed at its new version.
list modules;
